<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all padding="0" />
      <mj-text font-family="sans-serif" />
      <mj-class name="header" padding="10px 10px 20px 10px" background-color="white" />
      <mj-class name="header-title" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-size="24pt" font-weight="600" line-height="24pt" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="header-image" align="right" width="100px" />
      <mj-class name="header-issue" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />
      <mj-class name="header-date" align="right" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />

      <mj-class name="article" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="article-title" font-family="monospace" font-weight="400" font-size="14pt" />

      <mj-class name="summary" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="category-heading" font-family="monospace" font-weight="600" font-size="18pt" />

      <mj-class name="articles" padding="0 10px 0 10px" />
      <mj-class name="images" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer" padding="10px 10px 10px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer-unsub" align="left" />
      <mj-class name="footer-feedback" align="right" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body>
    <mj-container>

      <!-- Header -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="header">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column width="100%" vertical-align="middle">
            <mj-text mj-class="header-title">Newsletter del Lunes.</mj-text>
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-issue">Issue No. 37</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-date">22 Septiembre 2025</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>
      <!-- /Header -->

      <!-- Summary -->
      <mj-section mj-class="summary">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            
Buenas a todos,
</br></br>
Hoy es una edición Pythónica en suma, no os alarméis en la siguiente vuelvo a C++ puro. 
</br></br>
Debería buscar fuentes de Qt, pero muchas no explican trucos ni nada por el estilo, podría anotarlo como tarea buscar alguna cosa mas de qt.
</br></br>
También, podría hacer una encuenta para saber que tipo de materias os interesa, o escribirme directamente, o a la cara, como prefiráis.
</br></br>
Un saludo!

          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Images -->
      <mj-section mj-class="images">
        <mj-column>
          
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
      
      <mj-section>
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            <h2>Artículos</h2>
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Articles -->
			<mj-wrapper mj-class="articles">
				
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://levelup.gitconnected.com/mastering-pythons-asyncio-the-unspoken-secrets-of-writing-high-performance-code-3d7483518894">Mastering Python’s Asyncio: The Unspoken Secrets of Writing High-Performance Code | by Sohail Saifi | Level Up Coding</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Artículo muy pensado para los pythonisos para aprender algunos trucos de asyncio.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://medium.com/the-pythonworld/async-vs-threads-in-python-a-simple-mental-model-that-finally-made-it-click-4d890b989dc8">Async vs Threads in Python — A Simple Mental Model That Finally Made It Click | by Aashish Kumar | The Pythonworld | Jul, 2025 | Medium</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Siguiendo la línea, explicando la diferencia entre Async y Threads en Python.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://pythoninstitute.org/pcep">PCEP</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Aqui recurso para sacarse el Certified Entry-Level Python Programmer, entiendo que será como los certificados de Java pero para python, seguramente si busco encuentro el equivalente en C++.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://medium.com/@obaff/7-time-saving-ansible-features-youre-probably-not-using-3c35f7d63795">7 Time-Saving Ansible Features You’re Probably Not Using | by Obafemi | Medium</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Algunos truquitos para Ansible, que no vienen mal.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        

        
      </mj-wrapper>

      <!-- Footer -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="footer">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" padding-bottom="5px" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-unsub">Not interested? <a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Unsubscribe">Unsubscribe</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-feedback"><a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Feedback">Feedback</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>

    </mj-container>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
